@startuml
title Budget agent: evidence, decisions, and approval
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
start
:Trigger: scheduler, CLI or API;
:Deterministic input boundary\nsync FIRST, then load_state and measure pace;
if (No usable budget / period ended?) then (yes)
  :detect_recurring -> forecast_cash -> decide_signals -> log_advice;
  :Output boundary: no_budget / period_ended;
  stop
endif
:detect_recurring: refresh and diff streams;
:forecast_cash: checking range, bill dip and surplus;
if (Any category flagged?) then (yes)
  :Privacy input boundary\nfacts + current alerts + past advice/outcomes;
  note right
    Memory: current period alerts;
    up to five advice entries from this
    budget month and the preceding three.
    Categorization only counts missing categories.
  end note
  :LLM diagnoses each flag\none_time / seasonal / recurring;
  :LLM chooses each action\nalert / suggest_cuts / adjust_next_budget / no_op;
  :Deterministic output boundary: enforce rules;
  note right
    Invalid action after one schema retry, or known
    model outage: code-written fallback alert.
    Adjustment without recurring cause, or on
    free/saving line: downgrade to alert.
    no_op without prior equal-or-higher severity
    alert: downgrade to alert.
    Unknown exceptions can fail the run.
  end note
  :decide_signals: one call per signal, cap 3;
  :Output boundary: save alerts and advice\nSkip valid no_op; retain outcomes as memory;
  if (Adjustment proposals AND checkpointer?) then (yes)
    :interrupt: awaiting_user;
    :Human accepts or dismisses each proposal;
    :Resume without LLM\nWait again until all proposals decided;
  endif
endif
:decide_signals and log_advice if no overspend;
:Output boundary: run ok;
stop
note right
Recurring signals: new subscription, price increase, income change.
Keyed recurring replay guard; low-balance repeat policy.
Forecast errors do not stop overspend checks.
Cancellation suggestions never pause.
Clear signal and prompt facts before approval; save on exit.
Filter every checkpoint write, including failures.
end note
@enduml
